Where the register map comes from

src/ctucanfd_regs.h is the register map of the CTU CAN FD core. Its header
says it was written from the public CTU CAN FD IP core datasheet
(https://canbus.pages.fel.cvut.cz/ctucanfd_ip_core/doc/Datasheet.pdf) and from
the PCI wrapper layout that QEMU's ctucan_pci models.

docs/DESIGN.md says that what the QEMU 6.2 model leaves out or does
differently comes from reading hw/net/can/ctucan_core.c and ctucan_pci.c in
QEMU, confirmed where a register read could show it. It also says that the
rotating TXT buffer priorities follow the scheme Linux's ctucanfd driver
uses (section 5).

Third-party products

The QNX CAN DDK (libcan) and QNX SDP are QNX products under their own
licence and are not part of this repository.
